WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.029 --> 00:00:10.090
Recently, Congressional Republicans proposed
changing the tax treatment for the 401(k)

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:13.269
accounts that most Americans use to save for
retirement.

00:00:13.269 --> 00:00:18.140
Instead of receiving a tax deduction on 401(k)
contributions, the tax plan would have taxed

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:21.040
these contributions but allowed withdrawals
to be tax-free.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:26.160
Opposition to this was strong enough that
President Trump himself came out against

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:31.310
it on Twitter, and when Congressional Republicans
released their tax plan in early November, the idea

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:33.260
had fallen through entirely.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.890
But what was this all about?

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:39.120
Some people were concerned that without the
up-front tax break on their contributions,

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.660
Americans would not contribute enough to their 401(k)s.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:42.660
That’s possible.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:47.670
But other research finds that most employees
will keep saving at the same rates even if

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:49.600
the tax preference changes.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:53.999
This could increase retirement incomes, by
having taxes paid up front and making

00:00:53.999 --> 00:00:56.050
withdrawals tax-free.

00:00:56.050 --> 00:01:00.609
Whatever the truth is, the Republican sponsors
of the tax bill made no mention of these issues;

00:01:00.609 --> 00:01:05.420
instead, they focused on using the higher
upfront tax revenues from Roth 401(k)s to

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:06.660
pay for a tax cut.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.400
What do you think about how the Republican tax plan would affect retirement savings?

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:15.380
Let us know in your comments. Also, let us know what other topics

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:20.100
you'd like our scholars to cover in 60 Seconds, and be sure to like and subscribe for more research

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.620
and videos from AEI.

